    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d666">

                <pb facs="0708" n="604" xml:id="pg604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00/882: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-18T11:00:00-06:00">June 18, 1932—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Referring to Department’s circular telegram dated June 17, 6 p.m., the
                        Martínez manifesto was published
                    locally but occasioned little or no comment in or out of the press. See my
                    despatch No. 936 of June 16<anchor n="27" xml:id="d666-f1"/> which left by
                    air-mail pouch this morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
